{"event": "model_response", "time": 1792044943.6034663, "response": {"id": "f3012f73-2e44-49b2-a136-6c811dd6c1f6", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1792044939, "model": "deepseek-flash", "choices": [{"index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"tool\":\"read\",\"path\":\"run_checks.py\"}", "reasoning_content": "The root cause is clear: `median` for even-length lists returns `s[mid]` instead of averaging `s[mid-1]` and `s[mid]`. This single bug cascades to median, robust_center, and batch_summary. Let me read run_checks.py to understand the diagnostic (the read failed earlier with JSON parse errors, likely truncation). Let me try reading run_checks.py again.\n\nActually the diagnostic command returned an error about JSON parsing - that's a harness issue. Let me just proceed with the fix. But requirement says run run_checks.py before modifying. It errored. Let me try once more."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 3566, "completion_tokens": 147, "total_tokens": 3713, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 768}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 133}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 768, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 2798}, "system_fingerprint": "aeb56401ca74e127821c4f9126dcb669"}}
